# Privacy Policy for No Break Chain

**Effective Date:** May 11, 2026

Thank you for choosing to be part of our community at No Break Chain ("we", "us", or "our"). We are committed to protecting your personal information and your right to privacy.

This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our mobile application (the "App").

## 1. Information We Collect

No Break Chain is designed with privacy as a core principle. The vast majority of your data never leaves your device. 

### A. Locally Stored Data
All of your personal habit-tracking data is stored **locally on your device**. This includes:
*   **Habit Data & Logs:** Your created habits, check-in histories, badges, and break reason analyses.
*   **Photo Journals:** Any photos you take or upload for your habit check-ins are saved directly to your device's local application directory. **We do not upload, sync, or have access to your photos.**
*   **AI Forecasting:** The app provides "AI-powered predictions" regarding your habits. These predictions are calculated entirely on your device using local heuristics. **No habit data is ever sent to external AI servers or APIs.**

### B. Third-Party Services
To provide premium features and manage subscriptions, we use a trusted third-party service:
*   **RevenueCat:** We use RevenueCat to process and manage in-app purchases and subscriptions. RevenueCat may collect anonymous App User IDs, purchase history, and related transaction data to validate your premium status across devices. Please refer to [RevenueCat's Privacy Policy](https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy) for more information.

## 2. Device Permissions

To provide specific features, the App may request the following device permissions:
*   **Camera & Photo Library:** Required only if you choose to use the Photo Journal feature to document your habit check-ins.
*   **Notifications:** Required to send you Smart Reminders and alerts about your habit streaks.

You can enable or disable these permissions at any time through your device's system settings.

## 3. Data Security

Because your habit data, notes, and photos are stored locally on your device, their security primarily depends on the security of your device. We strongly recommend using secure lock screen methods (PIN, fingerprint, face recognition) to protect your device.

## 4. Children's Privacy

Our App does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13. 

## 5. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect new features (such as the addition of Photo Journals or AI Forecasting). We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.

## 6. Contact Us

If you have any questions or suggestions about our Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact us: o1e3studio@gmail.com
